Conclusion: Nethack is a lot fun :)

I installed it on one of my boxes a few years back, and couldn't figure
out how you could do anything in the game without cheating (coping
savegames).  I had no idea that the game was as deep as it was (I
figured the whole game was just repetitive dungeon crawling).  The
first time I got to the end of Sokoban (cheating the whole way) I found
an amulet and thought I won the game.  Yeah.

So anyway, I got back into it not so long ago, and found NAO.  I've now
fallen in love with the text-based version, and am proud to announce my
first ascension!

I play as intx13 on NAO... as I played I kept a log of the game,
important events that occurred and so forth.  For the record, this was
my second game playing as a valk, and the first in any nethack game in
which I made it past the quest.

If anybody's bored, here's my notes :)

